    "end.wishes_left": "{name} still has wishes left: {count}. Perhaps next time.",
    "end.carry_over": "Your shop, your coins and your keepsakes are saved: in the full game you continue right here, with night {night}.",
    "end.thanks": "Thanks for playing! Wishlist Spare Change for Spirits on Steam.",
    "end.thanks_full": "Thank you for keeping the shop. The spirits will remember you – and more nights are coming in the next updates.",
    "end.back": "Back to the menu",

    // Products (ids from data/products.ron). Hints are numbered from 1; any number of hints works.
    "product.rain_jar.name": "Jar of Rain Scent",
    "product.rain_jar.hint.1": "Something that smells of rain … Have you caught that smell of wet earth in a little glass jar with a lid?",
    "product.rain_jar.hint.2": "I miss the summer thunderstorms. Just to open a small jar once more and breathe in the rain.",
    "product.letter_paper.name": "Yellowed Letter Paper",
    "product.letter_paper.hint.1": "I never wrote to her … I need a few sheets to write on, old and a little yellowed, like the paper back then.",
    "product.letter_paper.hint.2": "Some words still need to be said. Have you some old letter paper – a few sheets for one last letter?",
    "product.music_box.name": "Little Music Box",
    "product.music_box.hint.1": "A melody … she always hummed it. A little wooden box that plays it when you wind the key and lift the lid.",
    "product.music_box.hint.2": "Tinkle, tinkle, like back then before falling asleep. A small box that plays a tune when it is wound up.",
    "product.pocket_watch.name": "Stopped Pocket Watch",
    "product.pocket_watch.hint.1": "I have lost my time. A small round watch on a chain, for a waistcoat pocket – it may have stopped long ago.",
    "product.pocket_watch.hint.2": "What time is it? What time was it? I would like a watch again, the kind that opens with a lid.",
    "product.wool_scarf.name": "Wool Scarf",
    "product.wool_scarf.hint.1": "I am so cold, for so long now. Something knitted from warm wool to wrap around my neck.",
    "product.wool_scarf.hint.2": "Something soft for my neck … long and woollen, the kind you wind round twice in winter.",
    "product.marbles.name": "Glass Marbles",
    "product.marbles.hint.1": "Will you play with me? The little glass balls you roll and flick across the floor!",
    "product.marbles.hint.2": "The colourful round ones with the swirl inside! Small, made of glass, a whole handful of them!",
    "product.tea_tin.name": "Empty Tea Tin",
    "product.tea_tin.hint.1": "The rattle of a tin in the morning … the little metal box where the tea leaves were kept. Empty is fine.",
    "product.tea_tin.hint.2": "The kitchen used to smell of bergamot. Have you a tea caddy, a tin with a tight lid that still smells of tea?",
    "product.faceless_photo.name": "Faceless Photograph",
    "product.faceless_photo.hint.1": "I no longer remember what I looked like. An old photograph, even a faded one where the faces are gone.",
    "product.faceless_photo.hint.2": "Was there ever a picture of us? A photograph in a frame, old and pale – I would know it.",
    "product.rusty_key.name": "Rusty Key",
    "product.rusty_key.hint.1": "Somewhere there is still a door for me. I need a key for it – an old one, it may be rusty.",
    "product.rusty_key.hint.2": "I am locked out, out of everything. If only I had a key again, even a rusty iron one.",
    "product.powder_compact.name": "Silver Powder Compact",
    "product.powder_compact.hint.1": "I must look pretty when he comes. A small round case with powder and a tiny mirror inside the lid.",
    "product.powder_compact.hint.2": "A little shine for my cheeks. Have you a powder compact, silver, that clicks shut?",
    "product.lavender.name": "Dried Lavender",
    "product.lavender.hint.1": "Grandmother's wardrobe always smelled like this. A bunch of dried purple flowers that keep the moths away.",
    "product.lavender.hint.2": "Something purple and calming. Dried flower stalks that smell sweet and fresh – they help me sleep.",
    "product.tin_soldier.name": "Tin Soldier",
    "product.tin_soldier.hint.1": "My brother had a whole regiment. A little soldier cast in tin, painted, standing to attention.",
    "product.tin_soldier.hint.2": "One was always missing, the drummer. A small toy soldier made of metal would complete the parade.",
    "product.ship_in_bottle.name": "Ship in a Bottle",
    "product.ship_in_bottle.hint.1": "I want to hold the sea in my hands again. A tiny sailing ship with its masts, inside a glass bottle.",
    "product.ship_in_bottle.hint.2": "My ship … she was so small at the end. Small enough to fit through the neck of a bottle.",
    "product.brass_compass.name": "Brass Compass",
    "product.brass_compass.hint.1": "Which way is home? I can't remember. Something round and brass with a needle that always points north.",
    "product.brass_compass.hint.2": "Something that always points north. A sailor's compass, so I can find my course again.",
    "product.fish_bone.name": "Fish Bone",
    "product.fish_bone.hint.1": "Mrrrow. Something that smells of the harbour – the bones a fisherman throws away after a meal.",
    "product.fish_bone.hint.2": "Prrr … the bony, crunchy thing. What is left of a fish when the meat is gone. Mrrp.",
    "product.ball_of_yarn.name": "Ball of Yarn",
    "product.ball_of_yarn.hint.1": "Mrrp! The round thing that rolls away! Wound from wool, with a loose end to catch.",
    "product.ball_of_yarn.hint.2": "Something soft to chase under the bed. A ball of knitting wool – it unrolls so beautifully.",
    "product.polishing_cloth.name": "Polishing Cloth",
    "product.polishing_cloth.hint.1": "My armour has lost its shine. A knight must gleam! I need a soft cloth to polish the metal.",
    "product.polishing_cloth.hint.2": "Rust, everywhere rust. Have you a cloth to rub it away until the steel shines again?",
    "product.gear.name": "Brass Gear",
    "product.gear.hint.1": "Something small and round with teeth all around – it makes the other wheels turn.",
    "product.gear.hint.2": "One little wheel is missing from the works, and nothing moves without it.",
    "product.clock_key.name": "Clock Key",
    "product.clock_key.hint.1": "A little key that does not open any door – you turn it, and time starts again.",
    "product.clock_key.hint.2": "Wind it up, wind it up … do you have the thing you wind it up with?",
    "product.little_bell.name": "Little Bell",
    "product.little_bell.hint.1": "Something that goes ting-a-ling when it moves, so you always know where it is.",
    "product.little_bell.hint.2": "A tiny silver voice on a ribbon. One shake and everyone looks round.",
    "product.leash.name": "Dog Leash",
    "product.leash.hint.1": "A long strap with a loop at one end – so a little someone never runs away again.",
    "product.leash.hint.2": "For walks. You hold one end, and at the other end something wags.",
    "product.snow_globe.name": "Snow Globe",
    "product.snow_globe.hint.1": "A whole winter in a glass ball. Shake it, and it snows on a tiny house.",
    "product.snow_globe.hint.2": "I miss snow. Have you got some that stays in your hand and never melts?",
    "product.seed_packet.name": "Seed Packet",
    "product.seed_packet.hint.1": "A little paper bag that rattles softly – put what's inside into the earth and wait for spring.",
    "product.seed_packet.hint.2": "Tiny sleeping things that wake up green if you give them earth and rain.",
    "product.watering_can.name": "Watering Can",
    "product.watering_can.hint.1": "Something with a long spout that gives thirsty things a drink, one gentle shower at a time.",
    "product.watering_can.hint.2": "Flowers can't walk to the rain. Have you something that carries the rain to them?",
    "product.storm_lantern.name": "Storm Lantern",
    "product.storm_lantern.hint.1": "A flame in a cage of glass and iron that no wind can blow out.",
    "product.storm_lantern.hint.2": "Out on the water at night I need a light that keeps burning in any weather.",
    "product.hair_ribbon.name": "Silk Hair Ribbon",
    "product.hair_ribbon.hint.1": "Something to tie my hair up for the dance. A long, smooth ribbon of silk.",
    "product.hair_ribbon.hint.2": "Blue, like the sky on the wedding day. A silk ribbon to tie a bow in my hair.",
    "product.wedding_veil.name": "Lace Veil",
    "product.wedding_veil.hint.1": "I never got to wear it, not once. The long white veil of lace a bride wears over her face.",
    "product.wedding_veil.hint.2": "Something white and light to walk down the aisle. Fine lace that falls over my hair.",
    "product.pressed_flower.name": "Pressed Flower",
    "product.pressed_flower.hint.1": "He gave me a flower once. I kept it pressed flat between the pages of a book.",
    "product.pressed_flower.hint.2": "A blossom that will never wilt – dried and pressed flat, the way you keep them in a book.",

    // Ghosts. ".the" is the name as the subject at the start of a sentence (with article where the language needs one).
